ggplot(map('france'), aes(long, lat, group = group, fill = region)) +
  geom_polygon() +
  coord_map(projection = "lambert", parameters = c(lat0 = 41.366005 , lat1 = 51.097523)) + scale_fill_manual(values = colors)

The trouble is that the order of the colors works one way when you use map() and another once it's been fortified into ggplot2. You should probably create a dataframe that translates between the region name and the color that you want. Fortify the map data and use dplyr to join the color data, then use scale_colour_identity to force the colors to what you have decided.

Post a better example and I think we can get there.

B

