Subject: geom_point isn't using data from my dataframe
Message-ID: <ILM_gsXPWM8.pev2IbbzCgAJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/ILM_gsXPWM8/m/pev2IbbzCgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I have a matrix that I converted to a dataframe using as.data.frame, it has several rows and columns and has column and row names.

When I plot like this it works:

ggplot(dataframe, aes(dataframe$"X",dataframe$"Y")) + geom_point()

When I plot like this I get a single point:

ggplot(dataframe, aes("X","Y")) + geom_point()

It seems that using the second method the actual data in the specified X and Y columns isn't being used and instead it's treating "X" and "Y" as factors hence the single data point. How can I fix this, Is there a problem with how my dataframe is formatted?

