MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mike,

ggplot uses non-standard evaluation so when you are giving it variables you don't quote them.
When you give it this:

ggplot(dataframe, aes("X","Y")) + geom_point()

Likely when you are plotting aes("X", "Y") it is literally plotting the factor X by factor Y and that would be a single point. It is ignoring your dataframe entirely.

This should work as intended:
ggplot(dataframe, aes(X,Y)) + geom_point()

If you want to quote them (for programming reasons) use aes_string()

ggplot(dataframe, aes_string("X","Y")) + geom_point()
ggplot(mtcars, aes_string("cyl", "mpg")) + geom_point() # this works

HTH,
B

