MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A hacky solution, which creates a legend for geom_smooth without fill (because se = FALSE) and then overlays a geom_smooth with the se = TRUE but without the legend. I suspect that grey is underlying all the colours and it's only visible with white. Try it your problematic code with "orange" and you'll see it looks different to normal orange.

ggplot(mpg, aes(displ, hwy, colour=class)) +

  geom_smooth(se = FALSE) +
  geom_smooth(show.legend = FALSE) +

  theme(legend.key = element_rect(fill = "white"))

Olivia

